WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.504
time went by, Wendy and her brothers began to forget about the life they had left.

2
00:00:17.724 --> 00:00:22.668
Their house in London, their parents, and Nana all seemed very far away.

3
00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:28.513
Wendy knew that the nursery window would always be open for her and her brothers to return.

4
00:00:29.474 --> 00:00:33.529
What worried her, though, was that John only dimly remembered their parents.

5
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.292
And Michael hardly remembered them at all.

6
00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:40.115
In fact, Michael thought of Wendy as his mother now.

7
00:00:41.396 --> 00:00:45.519
Wendy felt it was her duty to keep their old life from fading away.

8
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.083
She decided to make a test for her brothers—just like in school.

9
00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.585
The Lost Boys joined in as well.

10
00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:57.429
They all made small writing slates for themselves and sat around the table.

11
00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.052
They began writing and answering the test questions.

12
00:01:01.952 --> 00:01:06.914
Wendy created some "yes or no" questions, such as "Was Father taller than Mother?"

13
00:01:08.295 --> 00:01:15.598
She made up multiple choice questions like "What was the color of Mother's eyes: blue, green, or brown?"

14
00:01:16.919 --> 00:01:18.579
She also had them write essays.

15
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:26.463
The topics were "How I Spent my Last Vacation in England" and "A Detailed Description of the Nursery."

16
00:01:27.323 --> 00:01:32.010
Once the boys were finished, Wendy marked their little slates with a check mark if the answers were

17
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.212
correct. She'd make an X if they were wrong.

18
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:39.395
Needless to say, the answers the Lost Boys wrote were silly.

19
00:01:40.376 --> 00:01:44.259
They had never met Mother and Father or lived in the family's house in London.

20
00:01:45.419 --> 00:01:47.221
Still, they all had fun.

21
00:01:48.321 --> 00:01:52.504
Only it was sad to see how many X's John had on his test.

22
00:01:53.765 --> 00:01:56.167
Peter was the only boy who did not take the test.

23
00:01:57.047 --> 00:02:00.317
Except for Wendy, he hated all mothers.

24
00:02:01.577 --> 00:02:05.498
Peter was also the only boy on the island who couldn't write or spell.

25
00:02:06.278 --> 00:02:10.299
He felt he had more important things to think about—like his next adventure.

26
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.420
And adventures occurred every day.

27
00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.821
Sometimes it was a bear hunt.

28
00:02:16.681 --> 00:02:19.582
Other times it was a tangle with the pirates or the Indians.

29
00:02:20.482 --> 00:02:23.563
The little underground house was the quiet part of the children's life.

30
00:02:24.523 --> 00:02:26.824
The adventures outside were much livelier.

31
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:33.792
And though Wendy liked their quiet life at home, she admired the daring and carefree spirit of Peter

32
00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:34.493
and his gang.

33
00:02:35.374 --> 00:02:38.296
John and Michael both enjoyed the excitement of Neverland.

34
00:02:39.237 --> 00:02:41.698
But sometimes it was scary and dangerous.

35
00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.882
To please Wendy, Peter invented his own game.

36
00:02:46.802 --> 00:02:48.664
He would pretend not to have adventures.

37
00:02:49.645 --> 00:02:53.968
He pretended to live the life that John and Michael had had before coming to Neverland.

38
00:02:55.212 --> 00:02:58.473
He would catch a ball in the air or throw a ball to the other boys.

39
00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:05.375
Then they would push each other around, trying to get the ball away from each other.

40
00:03:06.175 --> 00:03:10.616
Peter also went for quiet walks, for what he called a "breath of air."

41
00:03:11.537 --> 00:03:14.518
Sometimes he just sat still, watching the sun go down.

42
00:03:15.818 --> 00:03:18.919
It was always an unusual sight to see Peter doing nothing.

43
00:03:19.759 --> 00:03:22.800
He looked so solemn during these times that one had to laugh.

44
00:03:23.648 --> 00:03:25.389
But this game did not last too long.

45
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:31.473
Pretty soon Peter lost interest in pretending to be a normal boy and went back to his adventures.

46
00:03:32.614 --> 00:03:36.517
When Peter went out alone, Wendy never knew quite what to expect.

47
00:03:37.758 --> 00:03:40.700
Often he'd say he had just gone out for a "breath of air."

48
00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:48.645
But, when Wendy went outside later, she would find something strange on the ground—a torn jacket with golden

49
00:03:48.705 --> 00:03:50.666
sleeves or an Indian war club.

50
00:03:52.247 --> 00:03:55.702
Other times, he would tell a story about how he shot a grizzly bear.

51
00:03:56.523 --> 00:03:58.004
But no bear was ever found.

52
00:03:58.924 --> 00:04:01.786
Sometimes he came home from his quiet walk with his head bleeding.

53
00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.950
Then Wendy would fuss over him and wash his cut with warm water.

54
00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.192
She was never quite sure what to believe.

55
00:04:10.153 --> 00:04:14.516
But there were some adventures that she knew to be true, because she was in them!
